The Command Breakdown
bash
echo "000c0c1500102ac000000a4845414c5448434845434b" | xxd -r -p | nc 154.57.164.63 30374
Table
Part	What it does
echo "..."	Outputs the hex string
xxd -r -p	Reverse hex dump — converts hex string back to raw binary bytes
nc 154.57.164.63 30374	Sends the raw bytes to the target server via netcat
Packet Structure (22 bytes total)
1. TC Transfer Frame Header (5 bytes)
Table
Bytes	Hex	Field	Value
0–1	00 0c	Version(0) + Spacecraft ID(12)	0x000c
2–3	0c 15	Virtual Channel ID(3) + Frame Length(21)	0x0c15
4	00	Frame Sequence Number	0x00
Frame Length = 21 means total frame size = 22 bytes (21 + 1).
2. Space Packet Header (6 bytes)
Table
Bytes	Hex	Field	Value
5–6	10 2a	Version(0) + Type(1=Command) + APID(42)	0x102a
7–8	c0 00	Seq Flags(3=Unsegmented) + Seq Count(0)	0xc000
9–10	00 0a	Packet Data Length = 11−1 = 10	0x000a
