Key Learnings
Table
Concept	Explanation
xxd -r -p	Converts plaintext hex → raw binary. -r = reverse, -p = plain hex without offsets
CCSDS Packet	Standard space communication protocol. Header fields are bit-packed
Big-endian	All multi-byte fields use big-endian (MSB first)
Frame Length − 1	CCSDS convention: length field = actual size − 1
APID	Application Process ID — identifies the onboard subsystem (42 = diagnostic app)
Why It Failed Before
Table
Mistake	Fix
Sent frame + space_packet (duplicated payload)	Send only frame (space packet is already inside)
Wrong TC header bit layout	0c 15 instead of 60 15 — VCID shifted correctly by 10 bits
Used recv() instead of recvall()	Server may not respond with newline; use nc or recvall
Alternative: Pure Python (No Shell)
Python
from pwn import remote

payload = bytes.fromhex("000c0c1500102ac000000a4845414c5448434845434b")
r = remote('154.57.164.63', 30374)
r.send(payload)
print(r.recvall(timeout=5))
r.close()
